§§ `Illustration (b) to section 405 — the warehouse operator, for section 407`

-- (b) A is a warehouse owner or warehouse operator. Z, going on a journey,
--     entrusts his furniture to A, under a contract that it shall be returned
--     on payment of a stipulated sum for warehouse room. A dishonestly sells
--     the goods. A has committed breach of trust.
--
-- The illustration is the section 405 case; section 407's Illustration then
-- names a warehouse owner or warehouse operator as an example of a person
-- entrusted with property FOR THE PURPOSE OF STORAGE FOR RENT OR CHARGE, and
-- the illustration's own words supply the rent — "on payment of a stipulated
-- sum for warehouse room". So this is the storage limb, on the statute's own
-- facts.
--
-- The section 405 limb is the SECOND: a dishonest disposal in violation of a
-- legal contract touching the discharge of the trust. Selling the goods is the
-- disposal; the contract to return them on payment is the contract violated.
--
-- Illustration (b) is also where the statute drops a word — it concludes "A has
-- committed breach of trust", without "criminal", where every other
-- illustration says "criminal breach of trust". Nothing turns on it.
`the warehouse operator's entrustment, Illustration (b)` MEANS `CBT Facts` WITH
    particulars           IS Particulars WITH
                               accused            IS "A"
                               date               IS "a date unknown"
                               time               IS ""
                               place              IS "A's warehouse"
                               `co-accused`       IS ""
                               `common intention` IS FALSE
    `entrusted by`        IS "one Z"
    property              IS "the furniture of the said Z"
    `property, in short`  IS "furniture"
    `purpose of the entrustment`
                          IS "under a contract that it shall be returned on payment of a stipulated sum for warehouse room"
    `entrusted with property` IS TRUE
    `entrusted with dominion over property` IS FALSE
    dishonestly           IS TRUE
    `misappropriates that property` IS FALSE
    `converts that property to his own use` IS FALSE
    `uses that property`  IS FALSE
    `disposes of that property` IS TRUE
    `any direction of law prescribing the mode in which such trust is to be discharged` IS FALSE
    `any legal contract, express or implied, which he has made touching the discharge of such trust` IS TRUE
    `intentionally suffers any other person to do so` IS FALSE

`the warehouse operator, Illustration (b)` MEANS `Aggravated CBT Facts` WITH
    particulars           IS `the warehouse operator's entrustment, Illustration (b)`'s particulars
    `breach of trust`     IS `the warehouse operator's entrustment, Illustration (b)`
    `for the purpose of transportation for hire` IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of storage for rent or charge` IS TRUE
    `being an employee`   IS FALSE
    `entrusted in such capacity` IS FALSE
    `in his capacity as a public servant` IS FALSE
    `his trade`           IS FALSE
    `his profession`      IS FALSE
    `his business`        IS FALSE
    `a banker`            IS FALSE
    `a merchant`          IS FALSE
    `a factor`            IS FALSE
    `a broker`            IS FALSE
    `an attorney`         IS FALSE
    `an agent`            IS FALSE
    `in his professional capacity, other than by way of a trade, profession or business mentioned in paragraph (b)` IS FALSE
    `in his capacity as a director of a corporation` IS FALSE
    `in his capacity as an officer of an unincorporated association` IS FALSE
    `in his capacity as a partner in a partnership` IS FALSE
