§§ `No aggravating capacity at all`

-- The charge sheet needs an `Aggravated CBT Facts` for every complaint, and
-- most complaints have no aggravating capacity in them. This wraps the Carl
-- Elias Moses entrustment AS CHARGED — the one the court held disclosed no
-- offence — with every capacity leaf FALSE, so it is the row's all-dark
-- control: nothing at all is made out on it, under any of the four sections.
`Carl Elias Moses, as charged, no aggravating capacity` MEANS `Aggravated CBT Facts` WITH
    particulars           IS `Carl Elias Moses, as charged`'s particulars
    `breach of trust`     IS `Carl Elias Moses, as charged`
    `for the purpose of transportation for hire` IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of storage for rent or charge` IS FALSE
    `being an employee`   IS FALSE
    `entrusted in such capacity` IS FALSE
    `in his capacity as a public servant` IS FALSE
    `his trade`           IS FALSE
    `his profession`      IS FALSE
    `his business`        IS FALSE
    `a banker`            IS FALSE
    `a merchant`          IS FALSE
    `a factor`            IS FALSE
    `a broker`            IS FALSE
    `an attorney`         IS FALSE
    `an agent`            IS FALSE
    `in his professional capacity, other than by way of a trade, profession or business mentioned in paragraph (b)` IS FALSE
    `in his capacity as a director of a corporation` IS FALSE
    `in his capacity as an officer of an unincorporated association` IS FALSE
    `in his capacity as a partner in a partnership` IS FALSE
    `in his capacity as a key executive` IS FALSE
    `of a corporation`    IS FALSE
    `of an unincorporated association` IS FALSE
    `of a partnership`    IS FALSE
    `in his capacity as a fiduciary` IS FALSE

§§ `Directives`

#EVAL (`charge under s 408` `Carl Elias Moses, as an employee of the company`)'s text
#EVAL (`charge under s 409` `Carl Elias Moses, as a director of the company`)'s text
#EVAL (`charge under s 408` `Carl Elias Moses, an employee but not entrusted as one`)'s refusal
#EVAL (`charge under s 407` `the warehouse operator, Illustration (b)`)'s text
#EVAL (`charge under s 409` `the Penang agent, in the way of his business`)'s text
#EVAL (`charge under s 409` `the Penang agent, not in the way of any trade, profession or business`)'s refusal

-- s 408. The employee, entrusted as one.
#ASSERT `offence under s 408` `Carl Elias Moses, as an employee of the company`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 408` `Carl Elias Moses, as an employee of the company`)'s `made out`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 408` `Carl Elias Moses, as an employee of the company`)'s text EQUALS "You, Carl Elias Moses, are charged that you, on or about 23 October 1989, at the premises of Trans-Pacific Credit Pte Ltd, Singapore, being an employee, and in such capacity being entrusted by Trans-Pacific Credit Pte Ltd (“the company”) with property, namely, the proceeds of the sale of 2,000 Overseas Union Bank Warrant 1994 received by you from DBS Securities Pte Ltd pursuant to a sale (per contract number 414270/501) of the said warrants, for the purpose of paying the same to the company, did dishonestly misappropriate the said proceeds, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 408 of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 408` `Carl Elias Moses, as an employee of the company`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
-- The employee is not a director, a public servant or anything else in s 409,
-- and the entrustment was not for transport or storage.
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 409` `Carl Elias Moses, as an employee of the company`)
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 407` `Carl Elias Moses, as an employee of the company`)

-- s 409(1)(d). The director.
#ASSERT `offence under s 409` `Carl Elias Moses, as a director of the company`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 409` `Carl Elias Moses, as a director of the company`)'s `made out`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 409` `Carl Elias Moses, as a director of the company`)'s text EQUALS "You, Carl Elias Moses, are charged that you, on or about 23 October 1989, at the premises of Trans-Pacific Credit Pte Ltd, Singapore, being a director of a corporation, and in such capacity being entrusted by Trans-Pacific Credit Pte Ltd (“the company”) with property, namely, the proceeds of the sale of 2,000 Overseas Union Bank Warrant 1994 received by you from DBS Securities Pte Ltd pursuant to a sale (per contract number 414270/501) of the said warrants, for the purpose of paying the same to the company, did dishonestly misappropriate the said proceeds, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 409 of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 409` `Carl Elias Moses, as a director of the company`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
-- A director is not thereby an employee, so s 408 does not lie on these facts.
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 408` `Carl Elias Moses, as a director of the company`)

-- THE NEGATIVE. The entrustment was not made in the employee capacity, so
-- s 408 fails on that leaf alone — and the refusal says which leaf. The
-- section 405 case underneath is untouched and s 406 still lies, which is the
-- whole point: the capacity is what the aggravated section adds.
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 408` `Carl Elias Moses, an employee but not entrusted as one`)
#ASSERT NOT ((`charge under s 408` `Carl Elias Moses, an employee but not entrusted as one`)'s `made out`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 408` `Carl Elias Moses, an employee but not entrusted as one`)'s text EQUALS ""
#ASSERT (`charge under s 408` `Carl Elias Moses, an employee but not entrusted as one`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 408 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of criminal breach of trust by an employee (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: being in any manner entrusted IN THAT CAPACITY with the property, or with any dominion over it — it is not enough that a person who happened to be an employee was entrusted."
#ASSERT `offence under s 406` (`Carl Elias Moses, an employee but not entrusted as one`'s `breach of trust`)

-- s 407. The warehouse operator, on Illustration (b) to s 405 and the
-- Illustration to s 407.
#ASSERT `offence under s 407` `the warehouse operator, Illustration (b)`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 407` `the warehouse operator, Illustration (b)`)'s `made out`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 407` `the warehouse operator, Illustration (b)`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about a date unknown, at A's warehouse, Singapore, the property hereinafter mentioned having been entrusted to you for the purpose of storage for rent or charge, and being entrusted by one Z with property, namely, the furniture of the said Z under a contract that it shall be returned on payment of a stipulated sum for warehouse room, did dishonestly dispose of the said furniture in violation of a legal contract, express or implied, which you had made touching the discharge of the said trust, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 407 of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 407` `the warehouse operator, Illustration (b)`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
-- A warehouse operator is not an employee of the person who stores with him.
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 408` `the warehouse operator, Illustration (b)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 409` `the warehouse operator, Illustration (b)`)

-- s 409(1)(b). Both columns of the paragraph, on the Penang agent.
#ASSERT `offence under s 409` `the Penang agent, in the way of his business`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 409` `the Penang agent, in the way of his business`)'s `made out`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 409` `the Penang agent, in the way of his business`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about a date unknown, at A's place of business, Singapore, in the way of your business as an agent, and in such capacity being entrusted by one Z of Penang with property, namely, $5,000 remitted to you by the said Z with directions to you to invest the same in Government securities, pursuant to an express or implied contract between you and the said Z that all sums remitted by the said Z to you shall be invested by you according to his direction, did dishonestly use the said moneys in violation of a legal contract, express or implied, which you had made touching the discharge of the said trust, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 409 of the Penal Code 1871."

-- Paragraph (b) needs BOTH columns. Take the trade, profession and business
-- away and the paragraph fails although he is still an agent — and nothing
-- else in s 409(1) catches him, because (c) excludes the very capacities (b)
-- names and he is in none of the others.
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 409` `the Penang agent, not in the way of any trade, profession or business`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 409` `the Penang agent, not in the way of any trade, profession or business`)'s text EQUALS ""
#ASSERT `offence under s 406` (`the Penang agent, not in the way of any trade, profession or business`'s `breach of trust`)

-- The all-dark control. The Carl Elias Moses entrustment as charged fails
-- section 405, and no capacity is asserted, so all three aggravated sections
-- refuse — and each refusal names BOTH of its rows, the capacity and the
-- section 405 case. This is the fixture the charge sheet carries by default.
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 407` `Carl Elias Moses, as charged, no aggravating capacity`)
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 408` `Carl Elias Moses, as charged, no aggravating capacity`)
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 409` `Carl Elias Moses, as charged, no aggravating capacity`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 409` `Carl Elias Moses, as charged, no aggravating capacity`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 409 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of criminal breach of trust by a public servant, or by a banker, merchant, agent, director, officer, partner, key executive or fiduciary (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: being entrusted with the property, or with dominion over it, in one of the capacities section 409(1) names — (a) as a public servant; (b) in the way of a trade, profession or business as a banker, merchant, factor, broker, attorney or agent; (c) in a professional capacity OTHER than one of those; (d) as a director of a corporation; (e) as an officer of an unincorporated association; (f) as a partner in a partnership; (g) as a key executive of a corporation, an unincorporated association or a partnership; or (h) as a fiduciary; committing criminal breach of trust in respect of that property (section 405) — run the section 406 charge on the same entrustment to see which of its elements failed."
